      "id": "sol.ahsme-1998-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The innermost radical is \\(N^{\\frac{1}{3}}.\\) The next is \\((N\\cdot N^{\\frac{1}{3}})^{\\frac{1}{3}}=N^{\\frac{4}{9}}.\\) The outermost is \\((N\\cdot N^{\\frac{4}{9}})^{\\frac{1}{3}}=N^{\\frac{13}{27}}.\\) Thus D is correct.",
